# suspend_gap_capabilities_setups: The capability check's flags where the host setup decides them, with enableArgumentBuffers set as QEMU's apple-gfx-mmio sets it: key 33 bit 0x20 (argument buffers) and key 42 bits 1 and 2 need isolation; key 33 bits 1 and 2 (large user and kernel tasks) need a memory map. Each case is one blob; which pass is the setup's own device info. Every setup runs it: the differences are behaviour (docs/testing.md 7.2).
